From 8320d1ee482cf7f0fc31891bd438fd4553601fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:24:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audit fix c: dated league clubs, page counts, card rows and
 id names

League_Stats pages: the Club / rights cell becomes a dated club (the
design change decided after the June 2006 audit): the clubs a player
appeared for in the period's closed results, in stint order joined with
"/", else his club on the page's label date (league_cards.club_on: the
2003-04 rules, then club_truth.holder), "<code> rights" only while a
club holds his unsigned draft rights, FA for no club, and no club or
league before he reached the NBA. Rows follow the registry id their card
link names, are sorted alphabetically, and the tracked-player and group
counts and the age caption are computed from the page. Closed seasons'
league pages, every season's bracket page and the league hub follow the
registry and the season list in every full write-back.

League cards: month and week rows use the age at the linked page's label
date and the clubs of the period's appearances; jersey, baseline, photo
and 2002-03 lookups read the bbr_id; club codes cover Charlotte and the
New Orleans/Oklahoma City Hornets and are never None. Playoffs.md states
its season's seeding rule from the rules file.

A player a result keys by his NBA id is registered (and, from the
2006-07 book, booked) under his careers-file name. The 2005-06 book and
every decision path keep their answers: club_on and club_truth are
unchanged for every other consumer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ExmaEeFA7X8K2pJG6n4PLH
